1
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:11,080
If I were a supervisor like you,

2
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:14,040
<i>I'd choose to protect my workers</i>

3
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:16,080
<i>instead of criticizing me for what I did.</i>

4
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:17,080
PREVIOUSLY

5
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:18,600
You're just a worker.

6
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:20,200
What right do you have to lecture me?

7
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:22,240
I thought you were a good supervisor.

8
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:24,160
<i>But now I know</i>

9
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:25,960
<i>you're not as good as I thought.</i>

10
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:27,640
If you want anything to eat,

11
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:29,440
I guess you'll have to make it yourself.

12
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:34,080
<i>But you need to finish
all your work first.</i>

13
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:36,240
<i>I don't trust Hathaya at all.</i>

14
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,800
I'm afraid Hathaya might try to hurt you.

15
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:42,800
Where did you get that much money?

16
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:44,520
I played cards all night

17
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:47,000
and won another 300,000, Mom.

18
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:50,200
So now we've got 800,000.

19
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:03,600
I started with 500,000
and made 300,000 in just one night.

20
00:04:05,040 --> 00:04:08,080
If I take all 800,000 and play again,

21
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:10,320
wouldn't I come back
with more than a million?

22
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:20,120
But what if I take
all 800,000 and lose it?

23
00:04:21,959 --> 00:04:25,920
Who could possibly be that unlucky?

24
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:30,120
No, no, 800,000 is already good enough.

25
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:38,320
Have a seat and wait a moment.
I'll make it for you right away.

26
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:54,920
Mom is quite old

27
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:56,880
and still has to stand and cook.

28
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:03,160
How many plates to cook, how many years
to work, just for a hundred grand?

29
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:10,720
I already have plenty of capital.

30
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:14,560
If I play one more night,

31
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:17,120
I should be able
to come back with a million.

32
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:29,160
Hey! Why aren't you working?

33
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:30,280
Sorry, boss.

34
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,400
My hand hurts. My glove is torn.

35
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:37,200
If your glove is torn,
why didn't you buy a new one?

36
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:39,880
Work as fast as I pay you.

37
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:44,120
Where are you going?

38
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:47,400
I'm giving him my gloves.
I only carry stuff, so I don't need them.

39
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:49,800
Stay out of it. Trust me.

40
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,240
What are you standing there for?
Get back to work!

41
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:56,040
I was going to get my hard hat, boss.

42
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:57,760
- Get your hard hat?
- Yes.

43
00:05:57,840 --> 00:06:00,320
I told you to wear it this morning.
Why did you take it off?

44
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:02,040
Since you took it off, don't wear it.

45
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:04,000
- Get back to work!
- Sorry, boss.

46
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:06,840
Oh, hey.

47
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:10,000
All you care about is work.
Don't you care about safety at all?

48
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:12,400
What are you going to do
if someone gets hurt?

49
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:13,880
You're just a worker.

50
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:16,160
Who are you to tell me how to do my job?

51
00:06:16,240 --> 00:06:19,080
Yes, I'm just your employee,

52
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:21,400
but we still have the right
to protect our own lives.

53
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:26,360
And I'm warning you now

54
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:30,000
because if there is an accident, you're
the one who will be held responsible.

55
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:34,400
I don't know what happened to you today,

56
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:36,840
but you can't take your anger
out on your workers.

57
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:38,200
That's not acceptable.

58
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:42,760
Honestly, I'm not worried about you,

59
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:44,600
but this project belongs to Grandpa.

60
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:46,200
I don't want to cause him any trouble.

61
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:57,800
Hello.

62
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:00,680
Damn it.

63
00:07:01,240 --> 00:07:03,120
- Max, watch the site.
- Yes, boss.

64
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:04,920
Yes.

65
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:08,320
Everyone, keep working!

66
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:17,200
DUANGJAI'S FOOD STALL

67
00:07:19,080 --> 00:07:20,440
Hathai.

68
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:23,320
Hathai. Hathai.

69
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,120
Hathai.

70
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:31,120
Did she go gambling again?

71
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:33,800
What am I going to do?

72
00:07:33,880 --> 00:07:36,640
Oh, Hathai! Good grief!

73
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:38,400
What am I going to do?

74
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,400
Mom!

75
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:43,000
Why are you shouting?

76
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:44,800
What's come over you?

77
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:46,080
Where were you?

78
00:07:46,160 --> 00:07:48,200
Taking a shower.

79
00:07:48,280 --> 00:07:49,480
Where are you going now?

80
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:52,680
I'm tired of listening to you nag me,

81
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:55,360
so I'm going to pay those people back
and get it over with.

82
00:07:56,800 --> 00:08:01,680
What a relief. You nearly gave me
a heart attack just now.

83
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:03,560
Thought you took the money to the den.

84
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:07,280
At first, I was thinking about it.

85
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:08,720
I...

86
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:11,160
I felt sorry for you.
I don't want to see you

87
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:13,920
standing over that stove cooking all day.

88
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:17,120
Then I thought about it again
and got scared I'd lose everything.

89
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:22,560
And I feel sorry for Hathaya too.

90
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:25,160
I know she's not exactly

91
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:27,560
living comfortably over there.

92
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:30,000
I want her to come back and live here.

93
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:34,880
I'm glad you think that way.

94
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:38,200
Wait for me to take a quick shower.
I'll go with you.

95
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:40,400
Mom!

96
00:08:40,480 --> 00:08:43,480
This isn't a wedding or an ordination.
What you're wearing is fine.

97
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:45,160
Oh, really?

98
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:47,920
Yeah. Then I'll put away
the pork and vegetables first.

99
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,480
- Yeah, yeah.
- Go put everything away.

100
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:51,720
I'll go get dressed.

101
00:08:58,200 --> 00:09:00,400
Aunt Duang, I need some boxed meals.

102
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:04,880
I'm about to go run an errand. Order
from the stall at the alley entrance.

103
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:08,120
Come on. I came here
specifically to support you.

104
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:10,720
I need 30 boxes for the kids
at the soccer field.

105
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:14,320
- Thirty boxes?
- Yes. Are you really turning that down?

106
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:18,320
Mom. Go ahead and make the food.
I'll go by myself.

107
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:21,920
Come on. Don't worry.

108
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,160
I've already made up my mind.

109
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:26,480
If I break my word, may I--

110
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:27,920
All right, all right.

111
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:31,640
I trust you. Go and come straight back.

112
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:34,360
Tonight, I'll order some barbecue for us.

113
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:38,720
Sounds good, Mom.
And put some of that barley tea

114
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:41,840
in the fridge so it's ice cold.
I'll be back soon.

115
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:42,800
You little...

116
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:46,360
- Have a seat and wait for your food.
- Okay, Aunt Duang.

117
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,320
Hey, Hathai.

118
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:11,520
Hey, Jim.

119
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:13,360
I heard

120
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:15,840
you won big the other day,
then you disappeared.

121
00:10:15,920 --> 00:10:18,680
Yeah. I won enough. I'm good.

122
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:21,000
What's your zodiac sign?

123
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:23,280
Leo. Why?

124
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:25,400
Same as me!

125
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:28,080
I just had my fortune read. They said

126
00:10:28,160 --> 00:10:31,920
Leos are on fire right now.

127
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:35,200
Our luck is through the roof!
Money's pouring in. I'm going back in

128
00:10:35,280 --> 00:10:37,080
to win another million or two.

129
00:10:37,160 --> 00:10:38,440
You coming?

130
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:41,440
You go ahead.

131
00:10:41,520 --> 00:10:43,280
- Suit yourself.
- Yeah.

132
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:01,800
Hey! Make some room!

133
00:11:01,880 --> 00:11:04,520
The new millionaire is here!

134
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:06,760
Come on! Deal the cards already.

135
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:11,120
My luck is on fire.

136
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:14,040
Come on!

137
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:28,040
Excuse me.

138
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:31,040
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

139
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:32,600
Do you work around here?

140
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:34,760
Yes.

141
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:38,120
I'm looking for someone who works
on this project. Do you know him?

142
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:40,080
Who are you looking for?

143
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:42,720
His name is Ramil. I'm his father.

144
00:11:42,800 --> 00:11:43,920
Do you know him?

145
00:11:45,040 --> 00:11:46,760
Ramil is my supervisor.

146
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:53,160
He is just up ahead.

147
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:55,400
I'm sure he'll be happy to see his father.

148
00:11:58,840 --> 00:12:00,120
Why do you think

149
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:02,760
he'll be happy to see me?

150
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:06,280
This morning, Ramil seemed
like something was bothering him.

151
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:08,480
I don't know what happened.

152
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:11,640
Maybe seeing his father
will help him open up.

153
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:23,400
What are you doing here?

154
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:25,040
You're not supposed to be here.

155
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:39,720
I know, but someone wants to see you.
He came here looking for you.

156
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:42,120
Who?

157
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:43,920
Your father.

158
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:05,880
Hathaya,

159
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:07,320
who did you bring to the boss?

160
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:09,760
Mr. Anon. Ramil's father.

161
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:48,040
I've been trying to call you.
You never answer my calls.

162
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:59,080
I missed you, so I drove over to see you.

163
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:02,680
Are you doing okay?

164
00:14:07,160 --> 00:14:10,360
That girl said something
was bothering you today.

165
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:14,880
If something's wrong, you can tell me.

166
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:17,880
I can help you solve any problem.

167
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:31,200
We haven't seen each other in months.

168
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:33,000
Got a girlfriend?

169
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:39,680
- Is there someone? I'll ask for her hand.
- What do you want?

170
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:50,040
I missed you.

171
00:14:51,080 --> 00:14:52,280
I wanted to see you.

172
00:14:55,280 --> 00:14:56,520
Miss me?

173
00:14:58,320 --> 00:15:00,040
Every time you call,

174
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:01,800
it's always about some mess,

175
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:04,400
some problem I have to fix.

176
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:09,880
When are you going to stop bothering me?

177
00:15:10,480 --> 00:15:11,880
Ramil, I'm sorry.

178
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:15,440
I never meant for everything
to turn out that way.

179
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:17,320
How many hundreds or thousands of times

180
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:21,720
do I have to hear you say
"I'm sorry" in my lifetime?

181
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:26,040
Dad. Where are you going?

182
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:27,400
I have to go work, son.

183
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:32,120
One day, I'll come back for you.
I'll buy you a big house.

184
00:15:32,880 --> 00:15:35,560
I don't want a house.
I want to stay with you.

185
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:39,480
‎I'm sorry.

186
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:41,840
Dad.

187
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:45,520
Stay with me, sweetheart.

188
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:48,040
Let your father go.

189
00:15:56,880 --> 00:15:59,640
You're a coward.
You ran away from your problems

190
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:01,960
and left your wife and son to suffer.

191
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:04,000
Take everything valuable.

192
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:09,960
What are you doing?!

193
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:12,760
Your husband owes my boss money.
Where is he?

194
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:15,520
He's gone. I don't know where he went.

195
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:18,720
He skipped out on his debt.
We're selling this stuff.

196
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:21,880
No. Please don't.

197
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:23,160
- Don't!
- Don't hurt Mom!

198
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:24,840
I won't give them to you!

199
00:16:24,920 --> 00:16:26,680
Hey, keep going.

200
00:16:27,640 --> 00:16:30,400
- No.
- Damn it.

201
00:16:31,840 --> 00:16:33,360
Let's go.

202
00:16:33,440 --> 00:16:35,040
No!

203
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:36,760
No!

204
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,520
Dad! Dad's back!

205
00:16:50,200 --> 00:16:52,000
I know everything.

206
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:54,040
I know what happened.

207
00:16:55,120 --> 00:16:58,560
Come live with me. I'll take care of you.

208
00:16:58,640 --> 00:17:00,000
Please.

209
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,319
I had to live in that house

210
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:10,960
like a servant.

211
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:14,160
I had to be his son's playmate

212
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,800
and tolerate their mistreatment.

213
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:18,960
I endured all of it.

214
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:21,280
Do you know why?

215
00:17:24,319 --> 00:17:27,760
Because I love Mom. I had to protect her.

216
00:17:28,720 --> 00:17:31,160
And what about you? Where were you?

217
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:33,480
You ran away and saved yourself.

218
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:36,960
You're selfish.

219
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:42,040
I didn't mean for it to happen.

220
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:44,960
I was deceived. I was cheated.

221
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:47,120
I didn't know it was a Ponzi scheme.

222
00:17:48,520 --> 00:17:50,080
I'm sorry, son.

223
00:17:55,520 --> 00:18:00,240
But let's not talk about the past anymore.
What's done is done.

224
00:18:02,720 --> 00:18:04,440
I won't hurt you again.

225
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:08,160
I want to be with you...

226
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:13,680
and make up for everything I did wrong.

227
00:18:39,560 --> 00:18:41,280
There's a business opportunity.

228
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:47,360
It doesn't take much money
to invest, but the profit is huge.

229
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:51,560
I want to invest in it,

230
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:55,280
but I don't have enough money.

231
00:19:00,800 --> 00:19:02,280
I just need to borrow it for a bit.

232
00:19:07,160 --> 00:19:09,720
Ramil, I promise
I won't mess up this time.

233
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:14,680
I'll pay you back every single baht,

234
00:19:14,760 --> 00:19:17,400
and I'll buy a huge house.
Bigger than Saksit's.

235
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:22,480
I only need to borrow 500,000.

236
00:19:26,480 --> 00:19:27,560
So in the end...

237
00:19:30,360 --> 00:19:31,760
it's about money.

238
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:45,960
That's all I'm giving you.

239
00:19:52,320 --> 00:19:54,160
And let this be

240
00:19:55,280 --> 00:19:57,000
the last time.

241
00:19:58,960 --> 00:20:00,280
After this,

242
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:03,800
don't come see me again.

243
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:10,120
I won't bother you anymore.

244
00:20:11,440 --> 00:20:12,640
I won't ask for anything again.

245
00:20:15,920 --> 00:20:17,680
Go back to work.

246
00:20:41,720 --> 00:20:43,280
Goodbye, sir.

247
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:05,880
Hathaya.

248
00:21:06,680 --> 00:21:07,520
I have to go.

249
00:21:12,320 --> 00:21:13,880
How dare you

250
00:21:14,720 --> 00:21:18,280
tell other people about my business?
You even brought him here.

251
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:22,680
You're talking about your father.

252
00:21:22,760 --> 00:21:24,280
None of your business.

253
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:29,960
I saw that something was bothering you.
I thought he might be able to help.

254
00:21:30,040 --> 00:21:33,680
If what I did upset you, I'm sorry.

255
00:21:34,360 --> 00:21:38,240
But you still shouldn't have spoken
to him like that. He is your father.

256
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,400
You must live

257
00:21:41,320 --> 00:21:42,760
in a pretty perfect world

258
00:21:44,400 --> 00:21:47,240
if you can imagine every family

259
00:21:47,320 --> 00:21:50,200
as a mother, father, and child

260
00:21:50,280 --> 00:21:51,600
hugging each other with love.

261
00:21:53,760 --> 00:21:54,800
You and I

262
00:21:56,200 --> 00:21:57,640
must be from different worlds.

263
00:21:58,560 --> 00:22:00,000
You don't know what it's like to only

264
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:03,320
have a father
when it's convenient for him.

265
00:22:07,360 --> 00:22:09,440
No matter how bad my life gets,

266
00:22:10,320 --> 00:22:12,440
I would never say something like that.

267
00:22:13,760 --> 00:22:18,000
Go. Get back to work. Go be a good person

268
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:20,800
in your perfect fantasy world.

269
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:36,520
Your life might actually
be better than mine.

270
00:22:51,520 --> 00:22:53,680
HATHAI

271
00:22:55,520 --> 00:22:59,600
Hathai, did your battery die or something?
Why can't I reach you?

272
00:23:14,440 --> 00:23:16,120
I've only got 500,000 left.

273
00:23:17,320 --> 00:23:19,040
I'd better stop now.

274
00:23:22,240 --> 00:23:24,200
Hey. Where are you going?

275
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:28,040
Where's that Leo luck now?
I'm down 300,000.

276
00:23:28,120 --> 00:23:30,880
Come on. You have to be patient.

277
00:23:30,960 --> 00:23:33,480
Leo has to fall before it rises.

278
00:23:33,560 --> 00:23:36,240
Then it shoots straight through the roof!

279
00:23:37,040 --> 00:23:38,920
Whatever. If you don't
want to play, go home.

280
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:40,200
I'm going in.

281
00:23:51,240 --> 00:23:52,880
Leo shoots to the top...

282
00:23:57,600 --> 00:23:59,320
Leo shoots to the top!

283
00:24:00,800 --> 00:24:03,240
Leo shoots to the top!

284
00:24:04,240 --> 00:24:06,880
Move!

285
00:24:06,960 --> 00:24:09,720
Leo is shooting to the top!

286
00:24:28,040 --> 00:24:31,320
Hathaya, that porridge smells so good.
It looks delicious too.

287
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:33,800
I made some for you too, Chaya.

288
00:24:35,480 --> 00:24:38,640
Thank you, my dearest big sister.
You're the sweetest.

289
00:24:38,720 --> 00:24:42,440
So, how has it been
working at the construction site?

290
00:24:44,720 --> 00:24:48,000
Oh no. Your hands are all rough.

291
00:24:48,080 --> 00:24:49,400
I can't accept this anymore.

292
00:24:49,480 --> 00:24:52,600
I'm going to talk to Grandpa and ask him
to move you back into the office.

293
00:24:53,240 --> 00:24:54,200
Chaya!

294
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:57,560
You don't have to. I can handle it.

295
00:24:57,640 --> 00:24:59,160
I don't want to bother Grandpa anymore.

296
00:25:00,960 --> 00:25:02,320
I feel sorry for you.

297
00:25:03,160 --> 00:25:05,560
If I get the chance, I'll talk to Grandpa

298
00:25:05,640 --> 00:25:06,960
and try to soften him up.

299
00:25:08,560 --> 00:25:10,560
Thank you so much, Chaya.

300
00:25:12,680 --> 00:25:15,000
And since you have to go
to the construction site soon,

301
00:25:15,080 --> 00:25:17,520
I'll take the porridge to Grandpa for you.

302
00:25:18,880 --> 00:25:20,320
Thank you.

303
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:22,680
Here.

304
00:25:22,760 --> 00:25:23,800
Alright.

305
00:25:31,680 --> 00:25:34,160
What is everyone doing?
The food still isn't here.

306
00:25:34,240 --> 00:25:35,600
Exactly.

307
00:25:35,680 --> 00:25:37,760
Hathaya is completely useless.

308
00:25:37,840 --> 00:25:39,600
She knows

309
00:25:39,680 --> 00:25:42,320
you have to eat
and take your medicine on time.

310
00:25:42,400 --> 00:25:44,200
I'll go deal with it.

311
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:47,360
Hot rice porridge is ready.

312
00:25:52,520 --> 00:25:55,320
Where's Hathaya?
Why are you carrying it yourself?

313
00:25:56,560 --> 00:25:58,720
The kitchen staff said
Hathaya woke up late.

314
00:25:59,440 --> 00:26:00,840
I was worried about you, Grandpa,

315
00:26:00,920 --> 00:26:04,120
so I made you some rice porridge
and prepared your medicine.

316
00:26:06,040 --> 00:26:07,360
How irresponsible can she be?

317
00:26:07,440 --> 00:26:11,200
If Chayanee hadn't gone
into the kitchen to make this for you,

318
00:26:11,280 --> 00:26:14,000
you'd probably be starving by now.

319
00:26:14,640 --> 00:26:17,120
Mom, don't criticize Hathaya.

320
00:26:17,720 --> 00:26:21,080
She has to work at the construction site,
so she must be exhausted.

321
00:26:22,280 --> 00:26:23,640
Grandpa, have some porridge.

322
00:26:29,080 --> 00:26:32,200
Does it need anything, Grandpa?
I can adjust it next time.

323
00:26:32,800 --> 00:26:33,600
It's delicious, sweetheart.

324
00:26:34,800 --> 00:26:37,000
What about that marketing plan

325
00:26:37,080 --> 00:26:39,480
I asked you to do? Is it finished yet?

326
00:26:40,120 --> 00:26:41,840
I was away from home for several days

327
00:26:41,920 --> 00:26:44,640
because I was working
on the marketing plan for you.

328
00:26:58,040 --> 00:26:58,880
Oh.

329
00:26:58,960 --> 00:27:00,200
Hathaya,

330
00:27:00,280 --> 00:27:02,120
you don't have to sit in the back today.

331
00:27:02,200 --> 00:27:04,240
Oh? Where's your boss?

332
00:27:04,320 --> 00:27:08,440
Boss is on a secret mission,
so he sent me to pick you up.

333
00:27:08,520 --> 00:27:10,080
Oh.

334
00:27:10,160 --> 00:27:11,520
But

335
00:27:11,600 --> 00:27:15,320
if your boss finds out I'm in
the front seat, you're in big trouble.

336
00:27:15,400 --> 00:27:17,080
Oh.

337
00:27:17,160 --> 00:27:20,600
If you don't say anything,
and I don't say anything,

338
00:27:20,680 --> 00:27:21,760
no one will ever know.

339
00:27:21,840 --> 00:27:22,800
Come on. Get in.

340
00:27:26,640 --> 00:27:27,760
Let's go.

341
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:45,280
RANONG PROVINCE

342
00:27:46,880 --> 00:27:49,280
I want to know who Hathaya's mother

343
00:27:49,360 --> 00:27:50,560
is living with

344
00:27:51,120 --> 00:27:52,040
and what she does

345
00:27:53,240 --> 00:27:55,560
and whether Hathaya's grandmother
is really sick.

346
00:27:56,720 --> 00:28:00,160
I don't believe what Hathaya told me.
I want the truth.

347
00:28:00,960 --> 00:28:03,800
According to the address
on the ID card Mr. Pichai gave me,

348
00:28:04,880 --> 00:28:06,400
it should be somewhere around here.

349
00:28:17,680 --> 00:28:19,240
Don't think I'm being nosy,

350
00:28:19,800 --> 00:28:21,960
but what kind of secret mission
is your boss on?

351
00:28:22,760 --> 00:28:24,640
To tell you the truth,
I don't know either.

352
00:28:25,760 --> 00:28:28,320
All I know is Mr. Pichai asked him
to help with something.

353
00:28:28,400 --> 00:28:30,920
Mr. Pichai is very kind to my boss.

354
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:32,840
When something comes up,
he calls him for help.

355
00:28:32,920 --> 00:28:35,000
What did Grandpa ask him to help with?

356
00:28:35,080 --> 00:28:36,120
Hit me!

357
00:28:36,200 --> 00:28:39,040
Come on, hit me! I said hit me!

358
00:28:39,120 --> 00:28:40,320
- Hit me!
- Don't do this!

359
00:28:40,400 --> 00:28:41,440
Let go of me!

360
00:28:41,520 --> 00:28:43,720
- Let go of me!
- Sir, calm down.

361
00:28:43,800 --> 00:28:44,960
What happened?

362
00:28:45,040 --> 00:28:47,360
Sir, please stop!
You'll get others hurt, too.

363
00:28:47,440 --> 00:28:48,560
Let go of me!

364
00:28:48,640 --> 00:28:50,280
I have no other choice!

365
00:28:50,360 --> 00:28:51,960
Let go of me!

366
00:28:52,040 --> 00:28:54,920
- Come here.
- Let go of me.

367
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:57,000
- Let go of me.
- Get out.

368
00:28:57,080 --> 00:28:59,080
Don't! Hey!

369
00:28:59,160 --> 00:29:01,040
Let go of my wife!

370
00:29:01,120 --> 00:29:02,720
Please calm down.

371
00:29:02,800 --> 00:29:05,640
You people need to stop
and get out of my house!

372
00:29:05,720 --> 00:29:06,760
I'm going inside!

373
00:29:06,840 --> 00:29:09,240
You built your houses on public land.

374
00:29:09,320 --> 00:29:11,200
The Subdistrict Office
is expanding the road.

375
00:29:11,280 --> 00:29:13,200
They sent several warning letters already.

376
00:29:13,280 --> 00:29:14,520
Time's up. The houses must go.

377
00:29:14,600 --> 00:29:16,320
We've lived here for decades!

378
00:29:16,400 --> 00:29:18,120
You can't just do this to us!

379
00:29:18,200 --> 00:29:19,520
That doesn't change anything.

380
00:29:19,600 --> 00:29:23,040
This is public land.
What you're doing is illegal.

381
00:29:23,120 --> 00:29:24,800
But the previous Chief

382
00:29:24,880 --> 00:29:27,600
allowed us to live here,
and now all of a sudden

383
00:29:27,680 --> 00:29:30,280
you people are trying to throw us out?
That's unacceptable.

384
00:29:30,360 --> 00:29:32,520
The houses come down, like it or not.
Just doing our job.

385
00:29:33,120 --> 00:29:35,480
- If you tear it down, I'll kill you!
- Yeah!

386
00:29:35,560 --> 00:29:37,440
- Go away.
- Get out!

387
00:29:37,520 --> 00:29:41,000
- Back off!
- You're dead!

388
00:29:41,080 --> 00:29:43,640
- Go away.
- Get out!

389
00:29:43,720 --> 00:29:45,560
Stop. Stop!

390
00:29:45,640 --> 00:29:46,960
Enough! Please stop!

391
00:29:47,040 --> 00:29:48,560
Stop! Enough.

392
00:29:48,640 --> 00:29:51,240
Please stop!

393
00:29:51,320 --> 00:29:52,640
This has nothing to do with you.

394
00:29:52,720 --> 00:29:53,920
How does this not involve me?

395
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:56,640
You drove him to jump in front of a car!

396
00:29:56,720 --> 00:29:59,040
I nearly killed someone
because of this problem.

397
00:29:59,120 --> 00:30:01,520
It's over now. You can leave.

398
00:30:01,600 --> 00:30:03,280
You really think you can handle this?

399
00:30:07,160 --> 00:30:09,240
I don't think this is going to end easily.

400
00:30:09,960 --> 00:30:12,240
Let me step in and help
both sides talk this through.

401
00:30:13,720 --> 00:30:14,680
Everyone.

402
00:30:17,080 --> 00:30:18,920
My name is Hathaya.

403
00:30:19,000 --> 00:30:22,520
I have no personal interest
in this matter.

404
00:30:22,600 --> 00:30:24,960
I just want to act as a mediator
and help both sides

405
00:30:25,040 --> 00:30:26,240
talk through the problem.

406
00:30:26,320 --> 00:30:27,160
Oh.

407
00:30:27,240 --> 00:30:30,720
Please help us.
We're being treated unfairly.

408
00:30:31,360 --> 00:30:32,200
Please.

409
00:30:32,280 --> 00:30:33,480
Please help us.

410
00:30:51,680 --> 00:30:52,800
Grandpa,

411
00:30:52,880 --> 00:30:54,800
come into the office first.

412
00:30:54,880 --> 00:30:57,400
I'm going to present
my PR and marketing plans.

413
00:30:57,480 --> 00:31:01,200
I guarantee you're going to be impressed.

414
00:31:02,440 --> 00:31:03,440
Let's go.

415
00:31:06,840 --> 00:31:09,640
The Subdistrict Office sent
written notices according to procedure.

416
00:31:09,720 --> 00:31:11,320
The residents were informed.

417
00:31:11,400 --> 00:31:13,320
Now that time's up, they're resisting us.

418
00:31:13,400 --> 00:31:16,360
That's a lie! You just showed up
and started tearing everything down.

419
00:31:16,440 --> 00:31:18,120
The evidence is right here.

420
00:31:18,200 --> 00:31:20,480
The dates are clear.
They got a month's notice.

421
00:31:20,560 --> 00:31:22,680
Don't believe them.

422
00:31:22,760 --> 00:31:24,480
We never received

423
00:31:24,560 --> 00:31:26,440
any warning letters.

424
00:31:26,520 --> 00:31:27,920
We only came here

425
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:29,800
after hearing they're
demolishing our homes!

426
00:31:29,880 --> 00:31:31,920
- That's why all of us came to protest.
- Yes.

427
00:31:32,000 --> 00:31:34,680
- Yes.
- We've lived here for so long.

428
00:31:34,760 --> 00:31:37,360
If it's really illegal,
why wait until now to evict us?

429
00:31:37,440 --> 00:31:39,000
- Right, everyone?
- Yes.

430
00:31:39,080 --> 00:31:40,120
That's right.

431
00:31:40,200 --> 00:31:41,640
Why didn't they make us leave before?

432
00:31:41,720 --> 00:31:43,240
You said you were going to help us.

433
00:31:43,320 --> 00:31:44,760
Then tell them

434
00:31:44,840 --> 00:31:46,080
they can't just throw us out.

435
00:31:46,160 --> 00:31:48,160
- Right, everyone?
- Yes.

436
00:31:48,240 --> 00:31:50,280
Tell them!

437
00:31:50,360 --> 00:31:52,320
Everyone, please listen.

438
00:31:53,080 --> 00:31:55,120
From what I can see in these documents,

439
00:31:55,200 --> 00:31:57,240
this land is public property.

440
00:31:57,320 --> 00:31:59,200
Homes cannot legally be built here.

441
00:31:59,280 --> 00:32:01,560
You work for the Subdistrict Office,
don't you?!

442
00:32:01,640 --> 00:32:03,720
Get out! Get out!

443
00:32:03,800 --> 00:32:06,920
Get out! Get out!

444
00:32:07,000 --> 00:32:08,680
Get out! Get out!

445
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:10,680
Please listen to me first!

446
00:32:13,560 --> 00:32:15,080
Listen!

447
00:32:15,160 --> 00:32:18,000
I have nothing to gain from either side.

448
00:32:18,080 --> 00:32:19,440
I'm only trying to help.

449
00:32:21,360 --> 00:32:23,240
I've been evicted plenty of times myself.

450
00:32:24,800 --> 00:32:26,440
My situation isn't that different.

451
00:32:31,320 --> 00:32:32,640
I really do want to help.

452
00:32:50,960 --> 00:32:52,040
Excuse me.

453
00:32:53,520 --> 00:32:55,160
Do you know

454
00:32:56,240 --> 00:32:57,600
where this person lives?

455
00:32:58,320 --> 00:32:59,360
No.

456
00:33:15,760 --> 00:33:16,720
Excuse me.

457
00:33:18,440 --> 00:33:20,600
Do you know this person?

458
00:33:22,680 --> 00:33:23,680
No.

459
00:33:25,760 --> 00:33:26,760
Thank you.

460
00:33:29,600 --> 00:33:31,360
My life has been difficult too.

461
00:33:31,440 --> 00:33:32,280
NO DEMOLITION!

462
00:33:32,360 --> 00:33:34,200
I understand what you're going through.

463
00:33:34,880 --> 00:33:36,160
Please let me help.

464
00:33:36,800 --> 00:33:38,240
Then what are we supposed to do?

465
00:33:38,320 --> 00:33:41,320
The houses were built illegally.
You have to move.

466
00:33:41,400 --> 00:33:42,880
Officer,

467
00:33:43,400 --> 00:33:44,920
you only care about tearing down homes.

468
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:46,640
Don't you feel any sympathy for them?

469
00:33:47,200 --> 00:33:48,880
Your salary

470
00:33:48,960 --> 00:33:51,280
comes from taxpayers.

471
00:33:51,360 --> 00:33:53,680
If you're going to talk to people
like that, think first.

472
00:33:54,800 --> 00:33:57,520
You should be helping them
find a solution.

473
00:33:57,600 --> 00:33:59,840
Don't take our taxes
and then leave people homeless.

474
00:34:00,480 --> 00:34:01,600
Hey.

475
00:34:01,680 --> 00:34:03,000
I like what she's saying!

476
00:34:03,080 --> 00:34:05,240
She's on our side!

477
00:34:06,760 --> 00:34:08,320
- Applause.
- Yeah!

478
00:34:08,400 --> 00:34:10,000
Here.

479
00:34:10,080 --> 00:34:12,080
Let's film this.

480
00:34:12,159 --> 00:34:13,560
People online need to see

481
00:34:13,639 --> 00:34:16,280
what these officials are doing to us.

482
00:34:16,360 --> 00:34:18,000
- Right?!
- Right.

483
00:34:18,080 --> 00:34:21,840
If you want to demolish their homes,
then you have to answer one question.

484
00:34:21,920 --> 00:34:24,000
Once you force them out,
where will they go?

485
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:28,920
Hello, everyone.

486
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:30,000
Hello.

487
00:34:30,080 --> 00:34:32,040
Hello, everyone.

488
00:34:32,600 --> 00:34:35,960
Our Subdistrict Office
has not ignored this issue.

489
00:34:36,040 --> 00:34:39,159
We've already prepared
a complete relocation plan.

490
00:34:39,880 --> 00:34:42,960
And most importantly, as the Chief here,

491
00:34:43,040 --> 00:34:44,520
I can assure you that

492
00:34:44,600 --> 00:34:47,159
once you move out, you will definitely
have somewhere to live.

493
00:34:47,239 --> 00:34:48,239
We don't want it!

494
00:34:48,320 --> 00:34:50,639
It's far away and as quiet as a graveyard.

495
00:34:50,719 --> 00:34:52,400
How are we supposed to make a living?

496
00:34:54,960 --> 00:34:56,360
Well...

497
00:34:56,440 --> 00:34:59,760
It may be quiet now,
but I believe that once all of you

498
00:34:59,840 --> 00:35:00,760
build homes there,

499
00:35:00,840 --> 00:35:04,120
and it becomes a larger community,
it won't be quiet anymore.

500
00:35:04,200 --> 00:35:05,120
Moreover,

501
00:35:05,200 --> 00:35:07,120
most of your neighbors

502
00:35:07,200 --> 00:35:08,600
have already moved out.

503
00:35:08,680 --> 00:35:12,160
We're asking everyone
in this community to cooperate

504
00:35:12,240 --> 00:35:15,720
for the sake of development
and the greater good.

505
00:35:17,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Chief,

506
00:35:18,960 --> 00:35:22,120
I agree with development
and considering the greater good.

507
00:35:22,800 --> 00:35:26,920
But I don't agree with using the majority
as an excuse to ignore the minority.

508
00:35:28,520 --> 00:35:31,920
True democracy isn't just
about listening to the majority.

509
00:35:32,520 --> 00:35:34,480
It also means listening to the minority.

510
00:35:34,560 --> 00:35:38,160
The majority should not be used
to pressure the minority into silence.

511
00:35:39,480 --> 00:35:41,320
We need to work together to solve this.

512
00:35:41,400 --> 00:35:44,720
We need to find the fairest solution.

513
00:35:46,400 --> 00:35:49,880
You know these houses are illegal.

514
00:35:50,560 --> 00:35:53,200
Yes. The evidence is clear.

515
00:35:53,760 --> 00:35:55,560
Everyone knows the houses are illegal.

516
00:35:58,360 --> 00:36:00,360
But you can't blame the residents alone.

517
00:36:00,880 --> 00:36:02,640
Officials neglected the situation

518
00:36:03,280 --> 00:36:05,920
and allowed them to live here
illegally for decades.

519
00:36:06,600 --> 00:36:08,280
That means the authorities

520
00:36:09,040 --> 00:36:11,800
failed in their duty too. Right?

521
00:36:11,880 --> 00:36:13,360
- That's right.
- That's right.

522
00:36:13,440 --> 00:36:14,680
The officials are at fault too.

523
00:36:14,760 --> 00:36:18,680
If the authorities had done
their jobs properly

524
00:36:18,760 --> 00:36:20,160
and fairly from the beginning,

525
00:36:20,240 --> 00:36:22,880
this problem would never
have reached this point.

526
00:36:23,520 --> 00:36:26,040
I don't want to place
all the blame on the villagers.

527
00:36:27,520 --> 00:36:29,520
The authorities need
to examine their actions

528
00:36:29,600 --> 00:36:32,200
and accept accountability
for their part in this too.

529
00:36:33,240 --> 00:36:36,320
- Yes!
- That's right!

530
00:36:36,400 --> 00:36:37,760
- True.
- Take responsibility.

531
00:36:37,840 --> 00:36:40,360
And from what I've heard,

532
00:36:40,440 --> 00:36:43,640
they're angry because the office
is rushing to tear down their homes.

533
00:36:44,520 --> 00:36:46,280
If they're relocated far away,

534
00:36:46,360 --> 00:36:48,480
how are their children
supposed to get to school?

535
00:36:48,560 --> 00:36:49,440
Where will they study?

536
00:36:49,520 --> 00:36:51,680
How are they supposed to earn a living?

537
00:36:51,760 --> 00:36:53,080
Where will they make money?

538
00:36:53,160 --> 00:36:54,720
If they can't make a living,

539
00:36:54,800 --> 00:36:57,360
they'll just have to pack up
their children and belongings

540
00:36:57,440 --> 00:36:59,560
and build another shack

541
00:36:59,640 --> 00:37:01,600
along a road or canal.

542
00:37:01,680 --> 00:37:03,760
Their lives will keep going
in the same cycle.

543
00:37:06,960 --> 00:37:10,640
I understand the need for development
and expanding the road.

544
00:37:11,240 --> 00:37:13,280
And I know allocating
land to the villagers

545
00:37:13,360 --> 00:37:14,920
would be difficult

546
00:37:15,000 --> 00:37:16,560
since land here is costly.

547
00:37:17,760 --> 00:37:19,120
Exactly.

548
00:37:20,080 --> 00:37:23,240
Since you understand that,
and everyone else understands it too,

549
00:37:23,320 --> 00:37:27,200
then we should all be moving
in the same direction.

550
00:37:27,280 --> 00:37:29,760
Please cooperate with the plan
we've already prepared.

551
00:37:36,360 --> 00:37:39,600
I won't let you keep living
a wandering life like this.

552
00:37:42,720 --> 00:37:46,080
I'll do my best to make sure
you can still earn a living around here.

553
00:37:50,120 --> 00:37:51,880
Thank you very much.

554
00:38:14,520 --> 00:38:17,800
This is the marketing plan I'm very proud
to present to you, Grandpa.

555
00:38:17,880 --> 00:38:21,440
I want to begin by promoting our housing
development through a campaign.

556
00:38:21,520 --> 00:38:23,440
We'll hire a famous actor

557
00:38:23,520 --> 00:38:26,000
as the face of the project.

558
00:38:26,080 --> 00:38:29,160
It'll make our development
the talk of the town.

559
00:38:37,840 --> 00:38:40,560
We're not a large company.

560
00:38:40,640 --> 00:38:42,640
We don't need to spend that much money.

561
00:38:44,560 --> 00:38:49,400
I want our brand
to become a national brand.

562
00:38:50,000 --> 00:38:52,840
Then, eventually, we can
take the company public.

563
00:38:52,920 --> 00:38:54,880
I'm not thinking only about today.

564
00:38:54,960 --> 00:38:57,680
I want us to look toward
the future, Grandpa.

565
00:38:59,920 --> 00:39:02,400
I agree with Chayanee.

566
00:39:02,480 --> 00:39:05,040
These days, you can't stay small

567
00:39:05,120 --> 00:39:06,760
and operate
like a family business forever.

568
00:39:06,840 --> 00:39:10,120
We need to grow into
a major national company.

569
00:39:12,160 --> 00:39:13,800
I put a lot of thought

570
00:39:13,880 --> 00:39:16,920
and effort into this for our family.

571
00:39:35,040 --> 00:39:38,680
Next time, don't make me come down here
and fix a problem like this myself.

572
00:39:39,200 --> 00:39:40,840
If this happens again,

573
00:39:40,920 --> 00:39:42,480
you're all fired.

574
00:39:43,080 --> 00:39:44,400
I'm sorry, Chief.

575
00:39:44,480 --> 00:39:45,440
Go!

576
00:39:48,400 --> 00:39:49,480
Oh.

577
00:39:50,480 --> 00:39:52,200
By the way, that young woman...

578
00:39:52,960 --> 00:39:54,760
Is she related to someone around here?

579
00:39:54,840 --> 00:39:56,040
No, Dad.

580
00:39:56,720 --> 00:39:59,280
That woman is Mr. Pichai's
eldest granddaughter.

581
00:40:00,320 --> 00:40:02,080
Oh!

582
00:40:03,040 --> 00:40:04,680
Mr. Pichai's granddaughter.

583
00:40:06,400 --> 00:40:09,600
No wonder she's so full of herself
and thinks she knows everything.

584
00:40:09,680 --> 00:40:11,160
I'd like to see whether

585
00:40:11,240 --> 00:40:13,360
she can actually deliver

586
00:40:14,040 --> 00:40:15,400
on what she promised them

587
00:40:16,640 --> 00:40:18,440
or whether she's all talk.

588
00:40:25,720 --> 00:40:27,080
I helped mediate

589
00:40:27,160 --> 00:40:31,120
until the Subdistrict Office agreed
to give people more time.

590
00:40:32,880 --> 00:40:34,320
What does that have to do with me?

591
00:40:34,400 --> 00:40:35,560
Exactly.

592
00:40:35,640 --> 00:40:38,840
The Subdistrict Office is demolishing
illegal homes. Everything is legal.

593
00:40:38,920 --> 00:40:40,760
That's the end of it.

594
00:40:40,840 --> 00:40:43,440
You shouldn't be interfering.

595
00:40:43,520 --> 00:40:45,080
Go back to work.

596
00:40:45,680 --> 00:40:48,080
I came to ask for your kindness, Grandpa.

597
00:40:48,960 --> 00:40:50,240
Hey.

598
00:40:50,320 --> 00:40:52,240
I told you to go back to work.
Are you deaf?

599
00:40:53,840 --> 00:40:56,840
The villagers are in trouble.
I think you can help them, Grandpa.

600
00:40:56,920 --> 00:40:58,320
Enough of your nonsense.

601
00:40:58,400 --> 00:40:59,320
Go!

602
00:41:00,360 --> 00:41:01,520
What do you want?

603
00:41:03,400 --> 00:41:06,160
I noticed there's an empty area
behind the project.

604
00:41:06,240 --> 00:41:08,040
It hasn't been used for anything.

605
00:41:17,800 --> 00:41:20,240
I think if we let
the villagers stay there,

606
00:41:20,320 --> 00:41:21,880
we can help them.

607
00:41:23,880 --> 00:41:26,400
Do you think our company
is some kind of charity?

608
00:41:27,680 --> 00:41:29,080
Absolutely not, Father.

609
00:41:29,160 --> 00:41:31,440
We can't let those people live there.

610
00:41:32,120 --> 00:41:35,160
They know how to manipulate
the system and take advantage.

611
00:41:35,240 --> 00:41:38,080
If they stay long enough,
they'll try to claim ownership.

612
00:41:40,960 --> 00:41:43,240
They would stay there as our workers.

613
00:41:46,800 --> 00:41:49,160
Most of them already work as day laborers.

614
00:41:49,240 --> 00:41:51,160
We can hire them to work for us.

615
00:41:51,240 --> 00:41:54,520
Our development is being rushed,
and we need more workers.

616
00:41:55,120 --> 00:41:56,280
Hathaya,

617
00:41:57,000 --> 00:41:58,880
once the project is finished,

618
00:41:58,960 --> 00:42:00,400
they'll be unemployed again.

619
00:42:00,480 --> 00:42:04,360
Once construction finishes, property
management will still need cleaners.

620
00:42:04,440 --> 00:42:07,560
and security guards.
These people are locals.

621
00:42:07,640 --> 00:42:09,440
I believe they could be
a great help to us.

622
00:42:09,520 --> 00:42:11,200
Now you've completely lost your mind.

623
00:42:11,880 --> 00:42:13,400
I disagree, Father.

624
00:42:13,480 --> 00:42:15,760
Those people drink, use drugs,

625
00:42:15,840 --> 00:42:18,520
and constantly cause trouble.

626
00:42:22,280 --> 00:42:24,960
The villagers who are being evicted
came to see Mr. Pichai.

627
00:42:25,040 --> 00:42:27,680
You brought them here
to pressure Father, didn't you?

628
00:42:27,760 --> 00:42:29,040
No.

629
00:42:30,440 --> 00:42:33,360
I know my words alone
may not be convincing.

630
00:42:34,040 --> 00:42:35,720
I wanted you to see them for yourself

631
00:42:35,800 --> 00:42:39,360
and understand how they feel,

632
00:42:39,440 --> 00:42:42,840
but whether you agree or refuse

633
00:42:43,600 --> 00:42:45,840
is entirely your decision, Grandpa.

634
00:42:45,920 --> 00:42:49,280
Father, don't go out there.
I'll go chase them away myself.

635
00:42:50,080 --> 00:42:51,480
If they refuse to leave,

636
00:42:51,560 --> 00:42:54,440
- I'll call the cops to drag them out!
- Grandpa.

637
00:42:54,520 --> 00:42:55,720
Grandpa.

638
00:43:04,440 --> 00:43:06,360
Sir, please.

639
00:43:06,440 --> 00:43:08,560
Sir, I want to work.

640
00:43:08,640 --> 00:43:11,960
- Sir, I want to work.
- We want to work.

641
00:43:12,040 --> 00:43:13,920
- Please.
- Everyone, please.

642
00:43:14,000 --> 00:43:15,120
- Calm down.
- Calm down.

643
00:43:15,200 --> 00:43:16,640
Please, calm down first.

644
00:43:17,160 --> 00:43:18,240
Sir,

645
00:43:18,800 --> 00:43:21,040
please let us stay here too.

646
00:43:21,120 --> 00:43:22,880
Please, sir.

647
00:43:22,960 --> 00:43:24,760
Sir, I swear

648
00:43:24,840 --> 00:43:27,400
I'll work as hard as I can.

649
00:43:27,480 --> 00:43:28,640
Please.

650
00:43:29,960 --> 00:43:32,000
Father, don't give in.

651
00:43:32,080 --> 00:43:33,440
Listen to me.

652
00:43:34,160 --> 00:43:35,920
If you hire these people,

653
00:43:36,000 --> 00:43:37,840
sooner or later, they'll cause trouble.

654
00:43:38,640 --> 00:43:41,600
And if they damage the project,
who's going to take responsibility?!

655
00:43:41,680 --> 00:43:43,320
I will.

656
00:43:43,840 --> 00:43:45,520
If anything goes wrong,

657
00:43:45,600 --> 00:43:47,160
I'll go home immediately,

658
00:43:47,240 --> 00:43:49,320
and I'll never bother you again.

659
00:43:53,040 --> 00:43:56,400
They're not your relatives.
You don't know them.

660
00:43:57,320 --> 00:44:00,840
What were you thinking,
risking your own life for them?

661
00:44:02,480 --> 00:44:04,200
Not everyone gets equal opportunities.

662
00:44:04,840 --> 00:44:06,400
I want to give them one.

663
00:44:18,400 --> 00:44:19,520
All right. Go.

664
00:44:20,640 --> 00:44:22,040
You can all go home now.

665
00:44:28,040 --> 00:44:30,440
Go pack up all your belongings.

666
00:44:31,800 --> 00:44:33,520
Then come back here and work for me.

667
00:44:34,160 --> 00:44:35,320
Build houses for me.

668
00:44:40,960 --> 00:44:43,240
Thank you so much, sir.

669
00:44:43,320 --> 00:44:45,160
We'll never forget your kindness.

670
00:44:45,240 --> 00:44:47,280
All right.

671
00:44:47,360 --> 00:44:48,960
Get up. There's no need to cry.

672
00:44:50,680 --> 00:44:52,520
I only ask one thing.

673
00:44:53,040 --> 00:44:55,200
Work hard and do your best.

674
00:44:55,800 --> 00:44:58,480
You've been given a good opportunity.
Don't waste it.

675
00:45:06,640 --> 00:45:07,840
Yay!

676
00:45:07,920 --> 00:45:09,760
We have jobs now!

677
00:45:09,840 --> 00:45:11,120
Thank you so much.

678
00:45:11,200 --> 00:45:14,200
- Thank you!
- Congrats.

679
00:45:14,280 --> 00:45:15,880
I'm so happy.

680
00:45:15,960 --> 00:45:17,560
Thank you.

681
00:45:17,640 --> 00:45:19,280
We're hired!

682
00:45:20,080 --> 00:45:22,960
I worked so hard on that
marketing plan to impress Grandpa,

683
00:45:24,000 --> 00:45:26,920
but Hathaya stole the spotlight
and grabbed all his attention.

684
00:45:27,000 --> 00:45:28,280
I hate her.

685
00:45:29,480 --> 00:45:32,760
Sweetheart, I warned you
not to underestimate her.

686
00:45:32,840 --> 00:45:36,280
She came back here
to steal our inheritance,

687
00:45:36,360 --> 00:45:39,880
and she's bringing in a whole group
of parasites to support her.

688
00:45:39,960 --> 00:45:43,360
Next, she'll take everything.

689
00:45:44,920 --> 00:45:47,640
I won't let her take what belongs to me.

690
00:45:48,400 --> 00:45:50,520
I'll get rid of these parasites myself!

691
00:46:13,000 --> 00:46:15,120
Hathaya asked Mr. Pichai for work

692
00:46:16,120 --> 00:46:17,880
to pay for her grandma's treatment?

693
00:46:21,680 --> 00:46:23,120
She looks perfectly healthy.

694
00:46:24,480 --> 00:46:25,600
Hathaya

695
00:46:26,200 --> 00:46:27,680
really did make the whole thing up.

696
00:46:28,200 --> 00:46:31,880
DUANGJAI'S FOOD STALL

697
00:46:32,800 --> 00:46:35,800
What are you thinking about?
You've been staring at me for a while.

698
00:46:36,840 --> 00:46:37,680
Oh!

699
00:46:37,760 --> 00:46:40,880
I was just thinking
your cooking must be delicious.

700
00:46:40,960 --> 00:46:43,080
It smells amazing.

701
00:46:43,160 --> 00:46:47,200
Spicy pork basil with a runny fried egg,
just like you ordered.

702
00:46:49,320 --> 00:46:51,280
That looks great.

703
00:46:56,320 --> 00:46:57,840
Don't forget this.

704
00:46:57,920 --> 00:46:59,680
You really know what I like.

705
00:47:00,280 --> 00:47:02,160
A fried egg needs chilies like this.

706
00:47:02,760 --> 00:47:06,760
That's how I like it too. But I'm old.
My granddaughter won't let me have it.

707
00:47:06,840 --> 00:47:08,080
She fears for my kidneys.

708
00:47:09,960 --> 00:47:10,920
Well,

709
00:47:11,600 --> 00:47:12,840
is your granddaughter not here?

710
00:47:14,360 --> 00:47:16,560
No. She went to Pathum Thani.

711
00:47:18,640 --> 00:47:20,200
What is she doing there?

712
00:47:23,320 --> 00:47:26,000
I don't want to talk about it.
It makes me angry.

713
00:47:28,520 --> 00:47:30,720
Sounds like this granddaughter of yours

714
00:47:30,800 --> 00:47:34,200
causes you a lot of trouble.

715
00:47:35,680 --> 00:47:37,520
If I could turn back time,

716
00:47:37,600 --> 00:47:39,560
I never would've let her go.

717
00:47:40,120 --> 00:47:42,880
Did your granddaughter go cause trouble

718
00:47:43,600 --> 00:47:45,200
or deceive someone?

719
00:47:45,800 --> 00:47:48,080
My granddaughter has never
deceived anyone.

720
00:47:48,160 --> 00:47:49,440
She's a good person!

721
00:47:50,320 --> 00:47:51,280
A good person.

722
00:47:51,360 --> 00:47:53,320
Of course she is.

723
00:47:53,400 --> 00:47:57,080
When I said someone deceived us
and caused us pain,

724
00:47:57,160 --> 00:47:58,760
I was talking about someone else.

725
00:47:59,800 --> 00:48:02,720
My granddaughter is as good as an angel.

726
00:48:07,520 --> 00:48:12,600
Why do you keep asking about
my granddaughter? What are you thinking?

727
00:48:12,680 --> 00:48:13,760
Are you after her?

728
00:48:13,840 --> 00:48:15,560
Grandma,

729
00:48:16,120 --> 00:48:18,960
of course not. I'm not from around here.

730
00:48:19,040 --> 00:48:20,920
I don't even know your granddaughter.

731
00:48:21,560 --> 00:48:25,400
What were you going to tell me?
What's she doing out in Pathum Thani?

732
00:48:27,040 --> 00:48:28,120
It's a long story.

733
00:48:29,520 --> 00:48:31,880
That's okay. I'm not in a hurry.

734
00:48:31,960 --> 00:48:34,040
If there's anything you want to tell me,

735
00:48:34,120 --> 00:48:35,920
I'm listening.

736
00:48:54,760 --> 00:48:55,840
Hey!

737
00:48:55,920 --> 00:48:57,360
Why are you setting those off?

738
00:48:58,040 --> 00:48:59,600
If something happens to her,

739
00:48:59,680 --> 00:49:00,720
you're going to jail!

740
00:49:00,800 --> 00:49:02,400
This has nothing to do with you.

741
00:49:02,480 --> 00:49:03,400
Stay out of it.

742
00:49:03,480 --> 00:49:04,600
Where's your daughter?

743
00:49:04,680 --> 00:49:07,320
Hathai took the money to pay you.

744
00:49:09,600 --> 00:49:11,360
Listen to this old lady.

745
00:49:11,440 --> 00:49:13,440
She says her daughter
brought us the money.

746
00:49:14,920 --> 00:49:17,080
- She did!
- If she paid her debt,

747
00:49:17,160 --> 00:49:18,840
I wouldn't even be here!

748
00:49:18,920 --> 00:49:21,760
I'm telling the truth.
She left with the money yesterday.

749
00:49:21,840 --> 00:49:23,520
She still hasn't come back.

750
00:49:23,600 --> 00:49:24,920
She hasn't paid us anything.

751
00:49:25,000 --> 00:49:26,960
You people are trying to mess with us?

752
00:49:34,240 --> 00:49:35,680
Hey.

753
00:49:37,400 --> 00:49:39,680
<i>And now we don't have
any money left to pay the debt.</i>

754
00:49:39,760 --> 00:49:41,000
<i>What are we going to do?</i>

755
00:49:41,080 --> 00:49:42,400
Mom, call Hathaya.

756
00:49:42,480 --> 00:49:44,280
Hathaya listens to you.

757
00:49:44,360 --> 00:49:47,320
<i>If she doesn't have the money,
she'll find a way. Please, Mom.</i>

758
00:49:47,400 --> 00:49:49,160
If any problem comes up,

759
00:49:49,240 --> 00:49:50,640
you have to leave this house.

760
00:49:50,720 --> 00:49:52,760
If you like Hathaya so much,

761
00:49:52,840 --> 00:49:54,360
then go see her.

762
00:49:54,440 --> 00:49:56,200
I don't have feelings for your cousin.

763
00:49:56,280 --> 00:49:57,920
<i>Then why are you
getting involved with her?</i>

764
00:49:58,000 --> 00:49:59,040
NEXT EPISODE

765
00:49:59,120 --> 00:50:00,200
<i>I hate her.</i>

766
00:50:00,280 --> 00:50:02,680
You're the Chief. You should be
at the Subdistrict Office.

767
00:50:02,760 --> 00:50:05,080
<i>Don't go around courting businesspeople</i>

768
00:50:05,160 --> 00:50:06,520
<i>for your own benefit.</i>

769
00:52:00,840 --> 00:52:02,800
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
